# React and Next.js

- Server Components by default. `"use client"` only when the component needs interactivity.
- Components get data through props. They never call Supabase or fetch directly;
  reads go through `features/<feature>/queries/`, writes through `features/<feature>/actions/`.
- Pages in `src/app/` only: read params → call queries → render feature components.
- Use shared primitives from `src/ui/` before creating new ones.
- Keys come from data ids, never the array index.
- Design loading, empty and error states. Never render nothing.
- Accessibility: every input has a label, every icon-only button has an `aria-label`,
  tap targets ≥ 44px, visible focus styles.

```tsx
// Bad: fetching and hardcoded copy in a presentational component
export function TopScorers() {
  const [rows, setRows] = useState([]);
  useEffect(() => { supabase.from("match_events").select("*").then(...) }, []);
  return <h2>Top Scorers 🔥</h2>;
}

// Good
export function TopScorers({ rows }: TopScorersProps): JSX.Element {
  if (rows.length === 0) return <EmptyState message={copy.topScorers.empty} />;
  return <LeaderboardList title={copy.topScorers.title} rows={rows} />;
}
```
